  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Considering UI Updates**\n\nI\'m currently focused on the UI redesign for \"DESMO STAV.\" I\'m prioritizing the color palette shift, moving away from dark greens to a charcoal black and a safety gold/warm yellow. This includes examining the use of #1A1A1A and #111111 for dark mode and exploring #E5A93B for the gold. My goal is to create a UI that\'s modern and trustworthy.\n\n\n**Implementing Home.tsx Update**\n\nI\'m now implementing the detailed content replacement for the home page. Focusing on `Home.tsx`, I\'ve decided a `multi_edit_file` approach is best given the extensive changes\342\200\224new services, timeline integration, and text updates are all coming. The goal is a seamless update reflecting the landscaping template content. I\'m also ensuring the correct color accents are applied.\n\n\n**Refining Code Generation**\n\nI\'ve shifted focus to a script to manage the extensive updates to `Home.tsx`. I\'m creating `rewrite_desmo_stav.js`, and this approach seems best for managing the content and design system updates. I am using the user\'s template mapping to do text replacements. This feels better than `multi_edit_file` now, since I can see all the changes. I\'ll focus on the Global Design System updates in conjunction with the content replacements.\n\n\n**Analyzing App.tsx Impact**\n\nI\'m now considering the implications for `App.tsx` and whether it requires updating alongside `Home.tsx`. I need to decide if I will be updating the links for the home page cards to their new routes or leaving the old routes for now. For the time being, I\'m focusing on overwriting `/src/pages/Home.tsx` entirely. I will avoid using `edit_file` to replace the whole content, it seems too big for that. I am also checking the background colors and card contents I need to change.\n\n\n"
